se((resolve) => server.close(resolve)); } const resumed = await dispatchNewsroomRepair({ assignmentId: predecessor, now: \"2026-07-19T05:02:00.000Z\", dataDir, contentDir, socketPath: join(root, \"missing.sock\") }); assert.equal(resumed.disposition, \"replay-ready\");","Prior research (content/posts/super-bowl-libra-rugpull-crisis.md, ni:///sha-256;B5bdUjaby2ux4g1DcYxtg4FObbMeTc7sDy1yQ1ihIQ4): keywords: [\"$LIBRA\"] categories: [\"Economy\"] tags: [\"$LIBRA\", \"Barstool Sports\", \"Dave Portnoy\", \"Javier Milei\", \"rugpull\", \"scam\"] references: - type: \"article-newspaper\"","Prior research (content/posts/super-bowl-libra-rugpull-crisis.md, ni:///sha-256;B5bdUjaby2ux4g1DcYxtg4FObbMeTc7sDy1yQ1ihIQ4): As the fallout continues, one key question remains largely unexamined: **where did the initial liquidity that fueled $LIBRAâ€™s meteoric rise come from?** And hereâ€™s where things take an unexpected turnâ€”Barstool Sports, its **Super Bowl betting operation**, and its outspoken founder **Dave Portnoy** may be closer to the story than anyone initially realized. ## The $LIBRA Collapse: A Timeline That Doesnâ€™t Add Up","Prior research (content/posts/super-bowl-libra-rugpull-crisis.md, ni:///sha-256;B5bdUjaby2ux4g1DcYxtg4FObbMeTc7sDy1yQ1ihIQ4): And hereâ€™s where things take an unexpected turnâ€”Barstool Sports, its **Super Bowl betting operation**, and its outspoken founder **Dave Portnoy** may be closer to the story than anyone initially realized. ## The $LIBRA Collapse: A Timeline That Doesnâ€™t Add Up To understand why this isnâ€™t just a run-of-the-mill crypto scandal, we need to look at the sequence of events:","Prior research (content/posts/super-bowl-libra-rugpull-crisis.md, ni:///sha-256;B5bdUjaby2ux4g1DcYxtg4FObbMeTc7sDy1yQ1ihIQ4): ## Dave Portnoy, Barstool, and the Role of Super Bowl Betting Liquidity Enter **Dave Portnoy**â€”a man who has made a career of blending sports media, gambling, and financial speculation. His **Barstool Sportsbook** was one of the major players in **Super Bowl betting**, a sector that saw billions of dollars in wagers this year.","Prior research (content/posts/super-bowl-libra-rugpull-crisis.md, ni:///sha-256;B5bdUjaby2ux4g1DcYxtg4FObbMeTc7sDy1yQ1ihIQ4): Enter **Dave Portnoy**â€”a man who has made a career of blending sports media, gambling, and financial speculation. His **Barstool Sportsbook** was one of the major players in **Super Bowl betting**, a sector that saw billions of dollars in wagers this year. We know Portnoy was involved in $LIBRAâ€™s promotionâ€”he admitted to receiving **six million $LIBRA tokens**, though he later claimed to have returned them after realizing the promotional arrangement was less transparent than he had hoped.","Prior research (content/posts/super-bowl-libra-rugpull-crisis.md, ni:///sha-256;B5bdUjaby2ux4g1DcYxtg4FObbMeTc7sDy1yQ1ihIQ4): The bigger question is: **Did Barstool Sports use liquidity from its cut as a sportsbook to artificially inflate the $LIBRA token before insiders cashed out?** Hereâ€™s why this matters:","Prior research (content/editorial-context/pipeline-context.json, ni:///sha-256;sf0l197yHija9SuEI99ZWbtEkdIsb92Tb5GIQEradWY): \"sourceId\": \"prior-art/agentic-newsroom\", \"digest\": \"sha256:f2efbcf0cf58ca651b4be4dc11899fef3ce7a95a003a10309126673bb0c99537\", \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Accountable Agentic Newsrooms Research Agenda\\ndescription: A research agenda for warrant-preserving editorial infrastructure, where evidence, attribution, authority, judgment, genre, legal risk, correction, and accountability remain distinguishable as claims move through humans, agents, tools, prose, metadata, feeds, and downstream summaries. Frames the problem as controlled delegation rather than autonomous publication, names fifteen research questions (editorial judgment as gates not functions, authority graphs, source-power modeling, mo...","Prior research (store/collapse-decolonization/the-meaning-of-omar-artan.json, ni:///sha-256;AWroBu3zxFggg9zntYLtOxEoxOTqI6JK-q7PPTdWca0): \"proposition\": { \"predicate\": \"summary\", \"object\": \"Omar Artan was already a hero before he came back to Somalia this week after being denied entry to the United States for the World Cup. Long before the controversy, he had become a household name in the country. As one former sports official told me, a warm welcome was guaranteed whenever he eventually returned to Mogadishu. But the decision by US immigration authorities to turn him away transformed the meaning of his homecoming. Somali journalists had spent the morning waiting for his flight from Istanbul to land. On the tarmac, a delegation of senior government officials waited patiently alongside us, flags in hand and many already che...","Prior research (store/decolonization/racism-at-the-world-cup-is-an-ugly-reality-how-to-understand-where-it-comes-from.json, ni:///sha-256;jjjwvs2KwZR05kEsGKeJdreLncin05Ul2K4djLNtofo): \"proposition\": { \"predicate\": \"summary\", \"object\": \"<figure><img src=\\\"https://images.theconversation.com/files/748358/original/file-20260716-57-4yz928.jpg?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&amp;rect=0%2C1%2C6452%2C4301&amp;q=45&amp;auto=format&amp;w=1050&amp;h=700&amp;fit=crop\\\" /><figcaption><span class=\\\"caption\\\">Racism was in the news once again at the World Cup. But it comes in many forms.</span> <span class=\\\"attribution\\\"><a class=\\\"source\\\" href=\\\"https://www.pexels.com/photo/a-man-sitting-on-a-football-field-5247136/\\\">Thirdman/Pexels</a></span></figcaption></figure><p>No African teams made it past the quarter-finals of the 2026 menâ€™s football <a href=\\\"https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worl..."],"accountableAttention":{"rule":"make-the-click-preserve-the-warrant","headlineMustPreserve":["attribution","modality","scope","uncertainty","correction state"],"forbiddenStrengthenings":["source claim to newsroom fact","may/could/alleged to does/did/proves","single case to trend","correlation to causation","reader demand to evidence"],"correctionSurfacePolicy":"Any later correction to a cited claim must propagate to body copy, headline, social cards, feeds, JSON-LD, and syndicated packets."},"constraints":["This packet is research intake, not a publishable article.","Only current-provider claims are admitted as source-bound factual evidence.","Prior-corpus excerpts are contextual leads until separately sourced and admitted.","Publication still requires a licensed editorial state, exact-manuscript judgment, and explicit publishing action."]}

CURRENT BODY:
As the World Cup final approaches this Sunday in New York City, atmospheric conditions have cast uncertainty over the match, which is slated to be held in an open-air stadium [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Large swaths of the United States, including the Midwest and the East Coast, have been blanketed by smoke from Canadian wildfires, forcing cities to confront hazardous air quality [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). While the air quality index in the region climbed to unhealthy levels on Thursday, triggering state alerts, the governing body for the tournament has not yet detailed a contingency plan for the event [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).

## A Gap in Institutional Preparedness

FIFA currently appears to have no standardized policy to implement adjustments or specific protocols for wildfire smoke, distinguishing it from other leagues that have already established such triggers [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). By contrast, the National Womenâ€™s Soccer League maintains a detailed policy that mandates game modifications or postponements when the air quality index reaches specific thresholds, such as 101 or 200 [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Requests for comment sent to FIFA regarding potential safety measures for players and fans went unanswered [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).

## Risks to Human Performance and Health

Physicians and environmental health experts have highlighted that exposure to wildfire smoke can cause symptoms such as coughing, throat irritation, and headaches, even among high-level athletes [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Because athletes perform intense physical activity, their exposure to air pollutants is higher, which can pose risks to their long-term respiratory health [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Vulnerable groups, including children, older individuals, and those with pre-existing conditions like asthma, also face increased dangers from the current air quality conditions [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).

## Watching the Atmosphere

Forecasters continue to track smoke patterns, with officials noting that conditions near the stadium remained in a moderate to unhealthy range as of Friday morning [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). While New York City has experienced hazy, orange skies throughout the week, the specific quality of the air on Sunday will depend on shifting wind patterns [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Until that day, the lack of a clear, disclosed plan from the tournament organizers leaves participants and observers to weigh the competing demands of athletic schedules and public health advisories [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).
